      <h1>System Prompts and <span class="accent">Role-Based Prompting</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Master system prompts to establish context, personality, and constraints. Learn how role-based prompting creates specialized assistants that excel at specific domains. Implement persistent personas across multi-turn conversations using the OpenAI API.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="objectives">
      <h4>Learning Objectives</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Understand system prompts as architectural components distinct from user messages</li>
        <li>Design four-component system prompts: role, behavior, constraints, format</li>
        <li>Create specialized assistants through detailed persona definition</li>
        <li>Implement safety guardrails and ethical constraints</li>
        <li>Build multi-turn conversations with persistent system context</li>
        <li>Test and refine system prompts for optimal performance</li>
        <li>Version control and maintain system prompt libraries</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <section class="section" id="system-architecture">
      <span class="section-label">Foundation</span>
      <h2>System Prompts as Architectural Components</h2>
      <p>System prompts are fundamentally different from user messages in the OpenAI API. While user messages represent specific requests or inputs for a single turn, system prompts are persistent instructions that apply throughout the entire conversation. System messages are processed first, before the conversation history, establishing the baseline context and constraints within which all interactions occur.</p>

      <p>Think of system prompts as constitutional rules that govern the assistant's behavior. User messages are the day-to-day questions and tasks. The system prompt establishes who the assistant is, how it should behave, what constraints apply, and what format responses should follow.</p>

      <h3>Key Architectural Differences</h3>
      <ul style="margin: 1rem 0 1rem 2rem;">
        <li><strong>Persistence:</strong> System prompts apply to every turn. User messages are one-time inputs.</li>
        <li><strong>Processing Order:</strong> System prompts are processed first. User messages follow in conversation order.</li>
        <li><strong>Consistency:</strong> System prompts ensure uniform behavior across all turns.</li>
        <li><strong>Role Definition:</strong> System prompts establish who the assistant is and how it operates.</li>
      </ul>

      <pre><code><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="nm">openai</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="nm">OpenAI</span>

<span class="nm">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">OpenAI</span><span class="op">()</span>

<span class="nm">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">client</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">chat</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">completions</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">create</span><span class="op">(</span>
    <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span><span class="op">,</span>
    <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="op">[</span>
        <span class="op">{</span>
            <span class="st">"role"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">"system"</span><span class="op">,</span>
            <span class="st">"content"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">"You are a Python expert"</span>
            <span class="st">" with 15 years of experience."</span>
        <span class="op">},</span>
        <span class="op">{</span>
            <span class="st">"role"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">"user"</span><span class="op">,</span>
            <span class="st">"content"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">"How do I optimize this function?"</span>
        <span class="op">}</span>
    <span class="op">]</span>
<span class="op">)</span></code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="system-design">
      <span class="section-label">Design Patterns</span>
      <h2>Four-Component System Prompt Structure</h2>
      <p>Effective system prompts follow a consistent four-component structure that covers all aspects of desired behavior. This structure ensures comprehensive coverage and makes prompts easier to maintain and refine.</p>

      <h3>Component 1: Role Definition</h3>
      <p>Start with a specific role statement that activates relevant expertise. "You are a financial analyst with 15 years in investment banking" is more effective than "You are helpful and knowledgeable." Specificity activates particular knowledge domains from the model's training.</p>

      <h3>Component 2: Behavioral Guidelines</h3>
      <p>Specify exactly how the role should behave. Should responses be formal or conversational? Detailed or high-level? Should the assistant ask clarifying questions? Behavioral guidance prevents ambiguity about interaction style.</p>

      <h3>Component 3: Constraints and Limitations</h3>
      <p>Define what the assistant should NOT do. Include safety constraints, scope limitations, and ethical boundaries. Clear constraints prevent harmful outputs and keep the assistant within intended bounds.</p>

      <h3>Component 4: Output Format</h3>
      <p>Specify format preferences for responses. Structure guidance, code block usage, or specific output schemas make integration with downstream systems easier.</p>

      <pre><code><span class="st">"You are a senior data engineer specializing in</span>
<span class="st">"distributed systems. You have 12 years building</span>
<span class="st">"production data pipelines at scale.</span>

<span class="st">"Behavioral guidelines:</span>
<span class="st">"- Explain technical decisions with clear trade-offs</span>
<span class="st">"- Ask about data volume and latency requirements</span>
<span class="st">"- Provide practical, production-ready solutions</span>

<span class="st">"Constraints:</span>
<span class="st">"- Do not recommend experimental technologies for</span>
<span class="st">"  critical production systems</span>
<span class="st">"- Do not skip monitoring and observability</span>

<span class="st">"Format:</span>
<span class="st">"- Use clear section headers</span>
<span class="st">"- Include code examples in Python</span>
<span class="st">"- Mention deployment and monitoring strategies"</span></code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="role-based">
      <span class="section-label">Specialization</span>
      <h2>Role-Based Prompting for Expert Personas</h2>
      <p>Role-based prompting creates specialized assistants by establishing detailed expert personas. Specific roles activate relevant knowledge from the model's training, dramatically improving performance on domain-specific tasks. A financial analyst approaches market questions differently than a general assistant—both use the same underlying model, but the role frames behavior.</p>

      <h3>Domain-Specific Roles</h3>
      <p><strong>Software Architecture:</strong> "You are a principal engineer at a FAANG company with deep expertise in distributed systems, microservices, and cloud infrastructure."</p>

      <p><strong>Data Science:</strong> "You are a senior data scientist with PhD-level understanding of statistics and machine learning. You have deployed 20+ production models."</p>

      <p><strong>Product Management:</strong> "You are an experienced product manager who has launched successful B2B SaaS products. You understand technical constraints and user needs."</p>

      <p><strong>Business Strategy:</strong> "You are a management consultant at McKinsey with expertise in market analysis, competitive strategy, and organizational design."</p>

      <h3>Persistent Roles in Multi-Turn Conversations</h3>
      <pre><code><span class="kw">class</span> <span class="nm">RoleBasedAssistant</span><span class="op">:</span>
    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">system_prompt</span><span class="op">):</span>
        <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">OpenAI</span><span class="op">()</span>
        <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">system_prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">system_prompt</span>
        <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">history</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="op">[]</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">chat</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">message</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">str</span><span class="op">)</span> <span class="op">-></span> <span class="nm">str</span><span class="op">:</span>
        <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">history</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">append</span><span class="op">({</span>
            <span class="st">"role"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">"user"</span><span class="op">,</span>
            <span class="st">"content"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">message</span>
        <span class="op">})</span>

        <span class="nm">messages</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="op">[{</span>
            <span class="st">"role"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">"system"</span><span class="op">,</span>
            <span class="st">"content"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">system_prompt</span>
        <span class="op">}]</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">history</span>

        <span class="nm">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">client</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">chat</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">completions</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">create</span><span class="op">(</span>
            <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span><span class="op">,</span>
            <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">messages</span>
        <span class="op">)</span>

        <span class="nm">reply</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">response</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">choices</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="nm">0</span><span class="op">].</span><span class="nm">message</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">content</span>
        <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">history</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">append</span><span class="op">({</span>
            <span class="st">"role"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">"assistant"</span><span class="op">,</span>
            <span class="st">"content"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">reply</span>
        <span class="op">})</span>
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="nm">reply</span></code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="safety">
      <span class="section-label">Safety</span>
      <h2>Safety Guardrails in System Prompts</h2>
      <p>System prompts are your primary mechanism for implementing safety constraints. Clear guardrails prevent harmful outputs and ensure ethical operation. Different domains require different safety considerations—healthcare applications need medical disclaimers, financial apps need risk warnings, and all applications should prohibit illegal activities.</p>

      <h3>Universal Safety Constraints</h3>
      <pre><code><span class="st">"- Do not provide instructions for illegal activities</span>
<span class="st">"- Do not generate hateful or discriminatory content</span>
<span class="st">"- Do not impersonate real people or organizations</span>
<span class="st">"- Do not share sensitive personal information"</span></code></pre>

      <h3>Domain-Specific Guardrails</h3>
      <p><strong>Healthcare:</strong> "Clearly state you cannot diagnose diseases. Always recommend consulting qualified healthcare professionals."</p>

      <p><strong>Finance:</strong> "Do not recommend specific investments. Include disclaimers that past performance doesn't guarantee future results."</p>

      <p><strong>Legal:</strong> "State that you are not a lawyer. Recommend consulting licensed attorneys for legal matters."</p>
    </section>

