    <section class="section" id="summary">
      <h2 class="key-concept-header">Key Takeaways</h2>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <h4>System Prompts as Architecture</h4>
        <p>System prompts are not conversational messages—they're persistent instructions that shape behavior. Understanding this architectural role is fundamental to effective LLM application building.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <h4>Four-Component Structure</h4>
        <p>Comprehensive system prompts include: role definition, behavioral guidelines, constraints, and format expectations. This structure ensures complete coverage of necessary behaviors.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <h4>Role-Based Knowledge Activation</h4>
        <p>Specific roles activate relevant knowledge from training. A "financial analyst" interprets information differently than a generic assistant using identical weights.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <h4>Safety Through Guardrails</h4>
        <p>System prompts are your primary safety tool. Clear constraints prevent harmful outputs and ensure ethical operation.</p>
      </div>
